-- module `strsib` — DELIBERATELY UNPARSEABLE, and unparseable in the ONE way
-- that also corrupts the LEXER's view: the string literal on the `tag` line is
-- never closed, so every character after it is swallowed into that string and
-- never becomes a `TIdent`.
--
-- ⚠️ THE OCCURRENCE MUST SIT *AFTER* THE OPEN QUOTE AND NOWHERE ELSE, or this
-- fixture proves nothing. A first version also carried
-- `import gooddefs.{strval}` ABOVE the `tag` line; the lexer reaches that line
-- fine, so a token-based mention scan still found `strval` there and the
-- discrimination check passed a build that was blind. The import is gone: the
-- only occurrence is on the last line, past the point the lexer loses.
--
-- A token-based scan therefore answers "this file does not mention
-- `strval`" and the F2 arm waves it through, silently dropping this occurrence.
-- `srcMentionsName` is a character scan for exactly this cell. This file
-- mentions `untouched` NOWHERE, so `partial.jsonl`'s positive control stays
-- discriminating.
tag = "unterminated

export strOther : Int
strOther = strval + 1
